    "field": "Biogeochemical cycles",
    "problem": "Interpreting the variability of oxygen isotopes in atmospheric CO\u2082 has been difficult due to confounding influences from both the carbon and water cycles, hindering its use for constraining global gross primary production, for which direct measurements do not exist at large scales.",
    "method": "This paper proposes a method for constraining global gross primary production by analyzing the decay time of El Ni\u00f1o-driven anomalies in a 30-year record of atmospheric CO\u2082 oxygen isotopes using a simple empirical model.",
    "task": "The task is to use the relationship between El Ni\u00f1o and the oxygen isotope composition of atmospheric CO\u2082 to constrain and revise estimates of global gross primary production.",
    "model": [
        "IsoGSM"
    ],
