            "target_entity_instance": "tropics",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "During El Ni\u00f1o/Southern Oscillation (ENSO) events, there are significant changes in the amount and intensity of rainfall in the tropics, especially over Southeast Asia and northern South America\u00b9\u00b9. Changes in the amount of precipitation also affect the \u03b418O value of water through the \u2018amount effect\u2019 and related processes\u00b9\u00b2. Figure 2 shows the correlation between the ENSO precipitation index\u00b9\u00b3 (ESPI) and the \u03b418O value of precipitation as hindcast by the IsoGSM model\u00b9\u2074 driven by reanalysis winds.",
